{
  "id": "S2E11",
  "season": 2,
  "episode": 11,
  "title": "Depart from Me",
  "showTitle": "The Hard Saying",
  "dates": "Saturday, February 6 – Monday, February 22, 2010",
  "logline": "Skye is in New Mexico and everyone else is in New Orleans, the Saints play for everything, Lent begins with a thumb, and sixteen days end at an airport curb.",
  "previously": [
    {
      "text": "In the Saab, Skye: “A car comes Saturday at six. Burbank, Albuquerque, and then some van with the show’s name taped in the window. Back the twenty-first.” … “Sixteen days.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "A card in a hand Jack knows: “American, Friday, 1:15. There’s a seat.” … “You’d be welcome.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "Behind the linen, Father Osei: “Come back when you can say it. I’ll be here. The light is on Wednesdays.”",
      "if": "s2e10_light==\"withheld\""
    },
    {
      "text": "Behind the linen, Father Osei: “You may come every Wednesday of your life,” … “I will be in this chair for every one of them; that is what the chair is for.”",
      "if": "s2e10_light==\"absolved\""
    },
    {
      "text": "Skye: “I told you I’m not mad at it.” … “I’m a little mad at it.”",
      "if": "s2e10_light!=\"withheld\" && s2e10_light!=\"absolved\""
    },
    {
      "text": "Skye, in the coat: “Go back Saturday. I’ll be on a plane. Nothing will be in the way.”",
      "if": "s2e10_light==\"withheld\""
    },
    {
      "text": "On the front steps, Doug: “Dude.” … “Super Bowl. My futon. Yusuf’s in.”",
      "if": "s2e10_light!=\"withheld\""
    },
    {
      "text": "Packing coats, Theo: “My mother’s under the burn. They’re saying rain Friday.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the dark, Skye: “I’m going to kiss you goodbye and you’re going to say *mm*.” … Jack: “I’ll say something better than *mm*.”"
    }
  ],
